 of $k$ and $p$.*\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $4$ | $2.132$ | $2.776$ |\n| $5$ | $2.015$ | $2.571$ |\n| $6$ | $1.943$ | $2.447$ |\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193279 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10.5 ± 0.9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191499} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10.5 ± 1.1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191500} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10.5 ± 0.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191501} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10.5 ± 0.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191502} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10.5 ± 0.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191503}] :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191498}] :question/math-academy-id "q-225026" :question/problem "Consider two paired samples of size $n = 50$ from the random variables $X$ and $Y$. Given that the mean of the differences $d_{i} = x_{i} - y_{i}$ is $d^(―) = 10.5$, and the variance of those differences is $s^{2} = 3^{2}$, find a $90%$ confidence interval for the population mean $μ$ of the difference $D = X - Y$. You may assume that the differences between the $i$th sample elements $X_{i} - Y_{i}$ are I.I.D random variables and each has the same distribution as $D$.\n\n*Hint: Given a random variable $T$ that has a student's $t$-distribution $T_{k}$ with $k$ degrees of freedom, the table below shows the $t$-scores $t_{k, p}$ such that $P(T > t_{k, p}) = p$ for some particular values of $k$ and $p$.*\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.010$ | $0.050$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $48$ | $2.407$ | $1.677$ | $2.682$ |\n| $49$ | $2.405$ | $1.677$ | $2.680$ |\n| $50$ | $2.403$ | $1.676$ | $2.678$ |\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Confidence Interval for Two Means" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048389 :topic/math-academy-id 3977 :topic/title "Confidence Intervals for Paired Samples: Unknown Variances"}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192674 :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193280 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.04" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191505} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191506} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.29" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191507} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191508} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191509}] :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191504} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "contains only positive values" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191511} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "contains zero" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191512}] :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191510} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191514} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.92" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191515}] :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191513} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "more" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191517} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "fewer" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191518} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the same number of" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191519}] :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191516}] :question/math-academy-id "q-225031" :question/problem "A factory has two locations, Location A and Location B. The factory produces $37$ different types of containers, and both locations manufacture all types.\n\nThe site manager wants to know if Location A produces more containers than Location B. He decided to sample the number of containers produced at both locations for all $37$ types and compute the difference $d_{i} = x_{i} - y_{i}$ for each type. Here, $x_{i}$ and $y_{i}$ give the number of type $i$ containers produced at locations A and B, respectively.\n\nAfter conducting their sample, he found that the average difference in the number of types produced was $d^(―) = 0.92$, and the variance of the differences was $s^{2} = 0.65^{2}$.\n\nFill in the missing information in the following statements and construct a $99%$ confidence interval for the mean difference $μ$ between the number of containers produced.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $P(T > 2.719) = 0.005$, where $T$ has a student's $t$-distribution with $36$ degrees of freedom.*\n\nThe end-points of the $99%$ confidence interval for the difference of the production rates, rounded to two decimal places, are approximately\n$0.92$ {{field-1}} {{field-2}}\nThe $99%$ confidence interval {{field-3}}.\nThis confidence interval suggests that Location A produces {{field-4}} containers compared to Location B.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193293 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191605} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.54" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191606}] :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191604} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "more" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191608} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "the same number of" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191609} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "fewer" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191610}] :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191607} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191612} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.04" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191613} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191614} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191615} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.02" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191616}] :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191611} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "contains zero" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191618} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "contains only positive values" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191619}] :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191617}] :question/math-academy-id "q-251472" :question/problem "A restaurant has two branches, Branch $1$ and Branch $2$. The restaurant offers its customers $40$ different dishes, and all dishes are offered in both branches.\n\nThe manager wants to know if Branch $1$ sells more dishes than Branch $2$. He decided to sample the number of orders at both branches for all $40$ dishes and compute the difference $d_{i} = x_{i} - y_{i}$ for each dish. Here, $x_{i}$ and $y_{i}$ give the number orders of dish $i$ at branches $1$ and $2$, respectively.\n\nAfter conducting the sample, he found that the average difference in the number of dishes sold was $d^(―) = 0.54$, and the variance of the differences was $s^{2} = 3.2^{2}$.\n\nFill in the missing information in the following statements and construct a $95%$ confidence interval for the mean difference $μ$ between the number of dishes sold.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $P(T > 2.023) = 0.025$, where $T$ has a student's $t$-distribution with $39$ degrees of freedom.*\n\nThe end-points of the $95%$ confidence interval for the difference in the number of dishes sold, rounded to two decimal places, are approximately\n$3.20$ {{field-1}} {{field-2}}\nThe $95%$ confidence interval {{field-3}}.\nThis confidence interval suggests that Branch $1$ sold {{field-4}} dishes compared to Branch $2$.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Confidence Interval for Two Means: Applications" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048389 :topic/math-academy-id 3977 :topic/title "Confidence Intervals for Paired Samples: Unknown Variances"}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192675 :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193396 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186192304} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186192305} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186192306} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186192307} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186192308}] :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186192303}] :question/math-academy-id "q-90278" :question/problem "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $E[X]$.\n$f(x) = \\frac{2}{x^{3